  "notes": "Official catalog program: 'Computer Science (BS) - Software Systems Track' (TSYS School of Computer Science, Columbus State University, Columbus, GA). Columbus State offers the BS in Computer Science only via named tracks (Software Systems, Games/Simulations Programming, Cloud and Web Services, Education, Enterprise Computing); there is no generic untracked CS BS. The Software Systems Track is the flagship/core computer science curriculum and is used here as the CS BS plan. Sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2022-2023 catalog 'Program Map' PDF (term-by-term guide), totaling 123 credit hours as published. The current 2026-2027 catalog page publishes a Program of Study (also 120 hours) but no term-by-term program map, so the 2022-2023 official map is the authoritative sequence source. The map states minimum grade of C required in major courses; it lists no formal course prerequisites beyond that, so all prereq lists are empty. Students must complete Area A (ENGL 1101, ENGL 1102, MATH 1001 or higher) before reaching 30 hours with a C or better in ENGL 1101/1102. CPSC 4000 Baccalaureate Survey is a required 0-credit course (required_zero=true). Current catalog program page: https://catalog.columbusstate.edu/academic-units/business/computer-science/computer-science-bs-software-systems-track/",
